      <h2>Official Railway RRB Photo &amp; Signature Guidelines (2026 Examination Standards)</h2>
      <p>
        The Railway Recruitment Boards (RRB) and Railway Recruitment Cells (RRC) under the Ministry of Railways, Government of India, enforce rigorous digital image validation rules across their unified application portals (including <strong>rrbapply.gov.in</strong> and regional zonal portals). Whether applying for <strong>RRB NTPC (Non-Technical Popular Categories)</strong>, <strong>RRB Group D (Level 1)</strong>, <strong>RRB ALP (Assistant Loco Pilot)</strong>, <strong>RRB Technician</strong>, <strong>RRB JE (Junior Engineer)</strong>, <strong>RPF Constable / Sub-Inspector</strong>, or <strong>Railway Act Apprentice</strong>, non-compliant photo files or invalid signatures trigger immediate portal rejection or application cancellation.
      </p>
      <p>
        This free, client-side <strong>RRB Photo &amp; Signature Resizer</strong> automatically formats your signature and admit card photographs to the official 2026 Railway standards. It enforces the exact <strong>30 KB – 70 KB</strong> file size range (or <strong>10–50 KB</strong> for Apprentice), scales images to the preferred <strong>350 × 450 px</strong> (photo) and <strong>240 × 80 px / 140 × 60 px</strong> (signature) dimensions, whitens dark paper backgrounds, and outputs clean JPG files with zero loss in visual clarity.
      </p>

