      <!-- Section 6: Common Railway Portal Rejection Reasons -->
      <h2>Top Reasons Railway Application Photos &amp; Signatures Get Rejected</h2>
      <ul class="mistakes-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Signature File Size Below 30.0 KB:</strong> Because scanned signatures on plain white paper contain very little color data, standard JPEG compression drops them to 10–20 KB. The Railway portal requires &ge;30 KB. Our engine automatically pads JPEG comment bytes to safely keep file size between 35 KB and 60 KB.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Signature in Capital Letters:</strong> Candidate signatures written in full block letters violate RRB verification norms and lead to immediate cancellation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dark or Textured Background on Photograph:</strong> Photos captured against colorful bedroom walls, outdoor trees, or with heavy shadow gradients behind the ears fail biometric inspection. Always use a pure white background.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Wearing Caps, Hats, or Tinted Sunglasses:</strong> Dark spectacles or headwear covering the forehead and ears are strictly forbidden by RRB instructions. Religious turbans are permitted provided full facial features are clearly visible.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Selfies and Distorted Mobile Angles:</strong> High-angle selfies captured with wide-angle smartphone lenses distort facial ratios. Use a studio passport portrait taken straight at eye level.
        </li>
      </ul>

